// markdownlint-cli2 options. Run via `npx markdownlint-cli2 "**/*.md"`, or let
// the lint workflow do it.
//
// USE markdownlint-cli2, NOT the `markdownlint` (cli v1) brew formula — they
// read DIFFERENT config files. cli2 is also what CodeRabbit runs, so a local
// run previews the PR gate rather than offering a second opinion.
//
// RULES live in .markdownlint.json and are still read from there; this file
// deliberately declares no "config" key so it cannot shadow them.
//
// Only TWO rules are disabled, each measured against this repo's actual corpus
// (10 stock findings across 3 files) rather than copied from elsewhere:
//
//   MD013 line-length (9 of the 10) — every hit is a Markdown TABLE row or a
//     guidance comment. A table cell cannot wrap at 80 characters without
//     becoming unreadable, and the 80-column convention predates side-by-side
//     diffs on wide screens. Disabled outright rather than raised, because a
//     limit that gets bumped each time a table grows is not a limit.
//
//   MD041 first-line-heading (1 of the 10) — pull_request_template.md starts
//     at `## Summary` on purpose. Its content is injected into a PR body, not
//     rendered as a standalone document, and a top-level `#` there would render
//     as an oversized heading above the description.
//
// Everything else in markdownlint's default set stays ON. Resist widening this
// list without a finding to point at: settimesdotca disables 18 rules, and that
// is justified there by a much larger and partly vendored corpus — it is not a
// template to copy.
{
  "gitignore": true,
  "ignores": ["**/node_modules/**"]
}
